  "body": "From the review of PR #115 (#71). The robust fit's inlier band is 3%·rho of the whole part (0.3 mm on D20, ~1.3 mm on a D100 flange) - 600 to 2600x SPINDLE_TOL (0.0005 mm). An off-centre line missing the axis by less than the band stays in the fit and still biases it (a tangential pin hole, asymmetric flat tessellation, features on a small diameter of a large part): ~0.5% of the area missing by 0.2 mm biases ~1 um, bringing back #71's false refusal on a correctly placed part. Fails closed (refusal, not a wrong cut).\n\nAlso: rotary coverage of the robust fit is vacuous - the rotary fixtures are pure revolves; add a keyed-bar rotary test.\n\nDone means: after convergence a final round with a tightened band (a few times the inliers' RMS, floored at the sagitta); pinned by a correctly placed shaft with a small tangential feature that passes; a keyed-bar rotary test.",
